    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: Computer Arithmetic\neditor_options:\n  chunk_output_type: console\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\noptions(digits=22) ## display values in 22 digits\n```\n:::\n\n\n# Integer\nAn integer $u$ is represented by  a vector of binary numbers $(d_0,\\ldots,d_{31})$ as follows:\n$$\nu=\\sum_{i=0}^{31} d_i2^i - 2^{31}.\n$$\nThe larguest integer is \n$$u^{max}=\\sum_{i=0}^{31} 1\\times 2^i - 2^{31}=2^{31}-1.$$\nThe smallest integer is \n$$u^{min}= - 2^{31}\\approx -(2^{31}-1).$$\n\nChecking the largest and smallest integers\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nas.integer(2^31)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n\n```\nWarning: NAs introduced by coercion to integer range\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] NA\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nas.integer(2^31 - 1)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 2147483647\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nas.integer(2^31 - 1) + as.integer(1) \n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n\n```\nWarning in as.integer(2^31 - 1) + as.integer(1): NAs produced by integer\noverflow\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] NA\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nas.integer(-(2^31 - 1))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] -2147483647\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nas.integer(- 2^31 )\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n\n```\nWarning: NAs introduced by coercion to integer range\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] NA\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nas.integer(- 2^31 -1 )\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n\n```\nWarning: NAs introduced by coercion to integer range\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] NA\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n# Floating point numbers\n\nA floating point number $x$ is reprented by a vector of binary numbers $(s,d_0,\\ldots,d_{t-1},e_1,\\ldots, e_{k-1})$ as follows:\n$$\nx = (-1)^s \\sum_{i=0}^{t-1}d_i2^{-i}\\times 2^{\\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}e_i2^i-2^k}.\n$$\nTypically, in double precision (64bits), $t= 52$ and $k=11$. The largest positive floating point number is roughly $2^{1024}$ and the smallest positive floating point number is roughly $2^{-1074}$. The numbers greater than $2^{1024}$ are overflow, called infinity. The numbers smaller than  $2^{-1074}$ are underlfow, treated as 0. \n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# checking the largest double precision floating-point number: \n2^1023\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 8.988465674311579538647e+307\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n2^1023+1\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 8.988465674311579538647e+307\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n2^1024\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] Inf\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n#smallest double precision floating-point number: > 2^(-1073)\n\n2^(-1074)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 4.940656458412465441766e-324\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n2^(-1075)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 0\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n# Rounding error \n\n## Computing sum: avoiding computing large + small\n    \n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n### demo of roundoff error: avoid large +- small\n\n\n# a number f0\nf0 <- 1 + 2^(-40)\n\nf0\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 1.000000000000909494702\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nf1 <- 1\ni <- 1\nwhile(i <= 2^12){     \n    f1 <- f1 + 2^(-52)   \n    i <- i + 1   \n}\n\nf1\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 1.000000000000909494702\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n#A method that will give your wrong answer\n\nf2 <- 1\ni <- 1\nwhile(i <= 2^13){     \n    f2 <- f2 + 2^(-53)   \n    i <- i + 1\n}\n\n\nf2\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 1\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# this difference is not due to number display in R:\nf0==f1\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] TRUE\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nf0==f2\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] FALSE\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n#R built-in function 'sum'\n\nf3 <- sum (c(1, rep (2^(-53),2^13)))\n\nf3\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 1\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nf1 == f3\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] FALSE\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nf4 <- sum (c(1, rep (2^(-54),2^14)))\n\nf4\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 1\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nf0 == f4\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] FALSE\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# a possible solution is to sort the numbers before adding\n\nf6s <- 0\ni <- 1\nwhile(i <= 2^14){     \n    f6s <- f6s + 2^(-54)   \n    i <- i + 1\n}\nprint (f6s)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 9.09494701772928237915e-13\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nf6 <- f6s + 1; f6\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 1.000000000000909494702\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\nLet's get a rough sense of mantissa in different bases:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n#base= exp(1) = 2.71\nlog(2^(-52))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] -36.04365338911715355152\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n1+ exp (-35)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 1.000000000000000666134\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n1+ exp (-37)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] 1\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n#based 10\nlog(2^(-52),base=10)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n[1] -15.65355977452702163077\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Computing exp (x): avoiding computing large - large\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nfexp <- function(x, debug=FALSE) \n{\n    i <- 0\n    expx <- 1\n    u <- 1\n    while(abs(u)>1e-20*abs(expx)) {\n        i <- i+1\n        u <- u*x/i\n        expx <- expx+u\n        if (debug){\n            cat(sprintf (\"Step %d: adding %f, exp(%f) = %f\\n\", i, u, x, expx))\n        }\n    }\n    expx\n}\n\nmatrix(c(exp(10),fexp(10)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n                        [,1]\n[1,] 22026.46579480671789497\n[2,] 22026.46579480671061901\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmatrix(c(exp(20),fexp(20)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n                        [,1]\n[1,] 485165195.4097902774811\n[2,] 485165195.4097902178764\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmatrix(c(exp(60),fexp(60)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n                            [,1]\n[1,] 114200738981568423454048256\n[2,] 114200738981568474993655808\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmatrix(c(exp(-1),fexp(-1)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n                         [,1]\n[1,] 0.3678794411714423340243\n[2,] 0.3678794411714424450466\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmatrix(c(exp(-10),fexp(-10)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n                            [,1]\n[1,] 4.539992976248485417315e-05\n[2,] 4.539992962303128097232e-05\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmatrix(c(exp(-20),fexp(-20)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n                            [,1]\n[1,] 2.061153622438557869942e-09\n[2,] 5.621884472130417612167e-09\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmatrix(c(exp(-50),fexp(-50)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n                            [,1]\n[1,] 1.928749847963917820563e-22\n[2,] 1.107293338289196981350e+04\n```\n\n\n:::\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n# See what's happening\nfexp (-50, debug = TRUE)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\nStep 1: adding -50.000000, exp(-50.000000) = -49.000000\nStep 2: adding 1250.000000, exp(-50.000000) = 1201.000000\nStep 3: adding -20833.3333